  (And then you posted data completely confirming it.)  The 
relevant intention was that the standard methods of dealing with 
a tough level (i.e. run away!, run away!) won't work.

  From the original post:

  "And you've spent all the time in the dungeons with mostly
smaller, much more easily escaped bodies of water.  A cursed 
potion of gain level won't save you now.  The up/down stairs
or a safe land area aren't x many moves away.  You can't 
cone-of-cold a safe area.  A cursed scroll of teleportation has 
no chance of helping you.  Any safe area you're in on the plane
of water can close in all around you until you're surrounded by
water.  You can't engrave Elbereth.  You don't have an infinite
supply of rocks.  You can't go up or down stairs to rest or get
something that will help.

  You will deal with the plane of water until you escape through
the portal, or until you die on the plane of water."

  That last statement sums up that it's do or die on the 
astral planes.  There's no retreating or bypassing and coming
back later with better spells or equipment.  You can't go back 
and get something you forgot in your stash.  You'll deal with 
them with what you have.

  That conclusion in the original post may not seem as inevitable
as it should based on the paragraph preceding it.  But I never
imagined anyone would argue with it at all, much less attempt
to argue with it by posting data confirming it.

  The point was that the player can't escape the level by -
     - confused reading of a scroll of teleport
     - read a cursed scroll of teleport
     - invoke the Eye of Aetheopica (Wouldn't it be fascinating 
       if this worked?)
     - invoke the Orb of Fate
     - go up stairs
     - go down a trap door
     - step in a hole another monster has dug.
     - zap a wand of digging downward
     - quaff a cursed potion of gain level


  You can't bypass the level, you've got to deal with it while
searching for the portal.  Doing two things at once, or rapidly
switching back and forth between two tasks is much harder than
doing one thing at a time.  

  Don't you agree that hard data of players dying on the Plane of
Water confirm "...until you die on the plane of water..."?


  Don't you agree that hard data of players dying on the Astral 
Plane confirm "...you escape through the portal..."?


